<!-- ============ 6 · EXPERIENCE ============ -->
<section class="page" id="exp">
  <div class="pad" style="padding-bottom:0;height:auto;">
    <h1 class="title" style="margin-top:.16in;">The Experience</h1>
    <div class="rule" style="margin-top:.16in;"></div>
  </div>
  <div class="stage">
    <!-- big taiko -->
    <div class="tile" style="left:0;top:0;width:4.55in;height:3.6in;background-image:url('data:image/jpeg;base64,');">
      <div class="chip">JASA's Tangerine Band</div></div>
    <!-- kimono tall -->
    <div class="tile" style="right:0;top:0;width:2.85in;height:3.6in;background-image:url('data:image/jpeg;base64,');background-position:center 30%;">
      <div class="chip">Singers on stage</div></div>
    <!-- bottom row of three -->
    <div class="tile" style="left:0;top:3.78in;width:2.42in;height:3.55in;background-image:url('data:image/jpeg;base64,');">
      <div class="chip">Festival games</div></div>
    <div class="tile" style="left:2.55in;top:3.78in;width:2.42in;height:3.55in;background-image:url('data:image/jpeg;base64,');background-position:center 28%;">
      <div class="chip">Omikuji fortunes</div></div>
    <div class="tile" style="left:5.10in;top:3.78in;width:2.30in;height:3.55in;background-image:url('data:image/jpeg;base64,');background-position:center 22%;">
      <div class="chip">Student bands</div></div>
  </div>
  <div class="mark fmark"><img src="data:image/png;base64,"><span class="wm">JASA</span></div>
  <div class="pagenum r">06</div>
</section>

<!-- ============ 7 · WHY SPONSOR ============ -->
<section class="page" id="why">
  <div class="pad" style="padding-bottom:0;">
    <h1 class="title" style="margin-top:.16in;">Why sponsor us</h1>
    <div class="rule" style="margin-top:.16in;"></div>
  </div>
  <div class="col">
    <p>Harumatsuri is entirely student-run and student-funded. Each year, JASA covers it through a mix of SGA funding, UMD football concessions, and sponsorships like yours! And every year, we hope to do more with Harumatsuri such as richer cultural programming, more performers and stalls, and keeping the festival free.</p>
    <p>Your support is what makes our Harumatsuri possible. Not only does your support directly fund our largest event that promotes Japanese culture, but it also puts your name in front of <strong>thousands</strong> of students.</p>
    <p>We would be thrilled to have you support us! A contribution of any size makes a difference, in whatever form works for you. I hope we can get in touch to work together on creating an unforgettable Harumatsuri!</p>
  </div>
  <div class="photo"><div class="bg" style="background-image:url('data:image/jpeg;base64,')"></div></div>
  <div class="photoB"><div class="bg" style="background-image:url('data:image/jpeg;base64,')"></div></div>
  <div class="callout">
    <div class="n">4,500+</div>
    <div class="t">total tickets sold last spring</div>
  </div>
  <div class="mark fmark"><img src="data:image/png;base64,"><span class="wm">JASA</span></div>
  <div class="pagenum r">07</div>
</section>

<!-- ============ 8 · BUDGET ============ -->
<section class="page" id="budget">
  <div class="pad" style="padding-bottom:0;">
    <h1 class="title" style="margin-top:.16in;">Where your support goes</h1>
    <div class="rule" style="margin-top:.16in;"></div>
    <p style="margin-top:.16in;max-width:5.4in;font-size:12pt;">Every dollar goes straight back into the festival. Here is where it is spent:</p>
  </div>
  <div class="cards">
    <div class="bc"><div class="ic"><svg width=".36in" height=".36in" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M3 11h18a9 9 0 0 1-18 0Z"/><path d="M9 3c-.7.7-.7 1.4 0 2.1s.7 1.4 0 2.1"/><path d="M14 3c-.7.7-.7 1.4 0 2.1s.7 1.4 0 2.1"/></svg></div><div class="tx"><h3>Festival food &amp; drink</h3><p>Takoyaki, daifuku, ramune and cotton candy; either catered from local vendors or freshly hand-made by our volunteers</p><p class="goal">This year, we hope to obtain more food warming appliances! As well as diversify cold items we can serve with a Japanese Kakigori machine</p></div></div>
    <div class="bc"><div class="ic"><svg width=".36in" height=".36in" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M2 20h20"/><path d="M4 20 12 4l8 16"/><path d="M12 4v16"/><path d="M9 20l3-6 3 6"/></svg></div><div class="tx"><h3>Equipment &amp; contracts</h3><p>The main stage, tents, tables and chairs, sound and lighting, and a generator</p><p class="goal">This year, we hope to expand our scale; we hope to change our tent number from 8 → 12!</p></div></div>
    <div class="bc"><div class="ic"><svg width=".36in" height=".36in" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M12 2v2"/><path d="M9 4h6"/><path d="M12 4C7 4 7 19 12 19s5-15 0-15Z"/><path d="M8.5 8h7M7.5 12h9M8.5 16h7"/><path d="M9 19h6"/><path d="M12 19v3"/></svg></div><div class="tx"><h3>Decorations &amp; props</h3><p>Lanterns, hand-painted banners, the Tanabata wishing tree, and hundreds of folded origami</p><p class="goal">Festival Haori Jackets are a must for any matsuri, so we are aiming to design them for this upcoming year!</p></div></div>
    <div class="bc"><div class="ic"><svg width=".36in" height=".36in" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><rect x="3.5" y="9" width="17" height="12" rx="1"/><path d="M2.5 9h19"/><path d="M12 9v12"/><path d="M12 9c-1-3-5-3-4 0"/><path d="M12 9c1-3 5-3 4 0"/></svg></div><div class="tx"><h3>Games &amp; prizes</h3><p>Materials for Shateki, goldfish-scooping and omikuji, plus the prize raffle that gives back to our community</p><p class="goal">To encourage ticket purchasing, it's important to have a variety of activities and games; we are aiming for more interactive games!</p></div></div>
    <div class="bc"><div class="ic"><svg width=".36in" height=".36in" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M9 18V6l9-2v12"/><circle cx="6.5" cy="18" r="2.5" fill="currentColor"/><circle cx="15.5" cy="16" r="2.5" fill="currentColor"/></svg></div><div class="tx"><h3>Performances &amp; programming</h3><p>Hosting taiko, kimono dance, and a dozen student acts on the main stage.</p><p class="goal">We are aiming for a larger stage to accommodate dance groups for this year! (+200%)</p></div></div>
  </div>
  <div class="mark fmark"><img src="data:image/png;base64,"><span class="wm">JASA</span></div>
  <div class="pagenum r">08</div>
</section>


<!-- ============ 10 · THANK YOU ============ -->
<section class="page" id="thanks">
  <div class="hero">
    <div class="bg" style="background-image:url('data:image/jpeg;base64,');background-position:center 55%;"></div>
    <div class="sc"></div>
  </div>
  <div class="body">
    <h1 class="title" style="margin-top:.14in;font-size:34pt;">Thank you</h1>
    <div style="max-width:5.7in;margin-top:.2in;">
      <p>We would really appreciate it if you could help support us. Donations of food or product are just as welcome. We will promote you as a headline contributor across our socials and promotions.</p>
      <p>Thank you for your time. We look forward to working together!</p>
    </div>
    <div class="sign">
      <div class="nm">Jason Lee</div>
      <div class="ti">Fundraising Chair @ JASA, University of Maryland</div>
    </div>
  </div>
